 class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[ἐν]θάδε κῆτε ὡ ἐν μακαρίᾳ \u003Cbr id=\"al2-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>[μ]νήμῃ \u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Γρηγώριος υἱὸς Πο\n                    \">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Γρηγώριος\">Γρηγώριος\u003C/span> υἱὸς \u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Πο\n                    \">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"patronym\" data-text=\"Πο\n                    \">\u003Cspan data-text=\"Πο\">Πο\u003C/span>-\u003Cbr id=\"al3-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/span> του π\u003Cspan class=\"supraline\" title=\"line above\">ρ\u003C/span>(εσ)\u003Cspan class=\"supraline\" title=\"line above\">β\u003C/span>(υτέρου) ζήσας ἔτη κβ´ \u003Cbr id=\"al4-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">4\u003C/span>[τ(ελ)]ευτᾷ δὲ ἐν \u003Cspan class=\"supraline\" title=\"line above\">Κ\u003C/span>(υρί)\u003Cspan class=\"supraline\" title=\"line above\">ῳ\u003C/span> μηνὴ Ἰ\u003Cspan class=\"supraline\" title=\"line above\">ου\u003C/span>(λίῳ) \u003Cbr id=\"al5-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">5\u003C/span>ἰν\u003Cspan class=\"intraline\" title=\"line through\">δ\u003C/span>(ικτιῶνος) η´ \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>",{"author":3,"date":4,"citedRange":117,"ptr":118,"ref":120,"inscriptionDate":4,"title":2,"citation":5,"uri":6,"year":4},"92 n.20",{"target":119},"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/6KPB9V5B",{"_":121,"target":121},"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001787",2006,{"file":124,"uri":124,"title":125,"status":126,"editions":128,"editionAuthor":135,"type":136,"objectType":137,"material":138,"condition":87,"layoutDesc":152,"handNote":156,"date":237,"places":242,"geo":250,"country":77,"provenance":244,"provenanceGeo":254,"region":81,"settlement":244,"repository":257,"idno":261,"textLang":264,"tmNumber":130,"facsimile":266,"letterHeights":273,"publications":311,"zotero":314,"keywords":317,"html":325,"bibl":326,"bulletinDateSort":122,"citedRangeSort":329,"languageSort":89,"materialSort":139,"typeSort":34},"ISic003337","Funerary inscription for Eirena",{"_":127},"edited",[129,131,132,133,134],{"_":130,"type":16},"645584",{"type":18},{"type":20},{"type":22},{"type":25},null,{"_":34,"ana":35,"ref":36},{"_":38,"ana":39,"ref":40},{"_":139,"ana":140,"type":141,"subtype":142,"resp":144,"ref":47,"placeName":145},"Very fine-grained, veined, white marble, likely Pavonazzetto. Digital microscopy: indistinguishable fabric. Scribbly veins, maybe a limestone (identification based on pXRF, digital microscopy)\n","#material.inorganic.stone.metamorphic_rock.marble.calcitic_marble.Pavonazzetto","stone.marble",[143],"Pavonazzetto","#Coccato",{"type":146,"ref":147,"location":150},"provenance",{"_":148,"target":149},"Bakakale","https://www.geonames.org/12207392/iscehisar-bucagi.html",{"geo":151},"38.86194,30.75028",{"layout":153},{"p":154,"rs":155,"damage":87},"Ten lines of Greek filling the available space, decreasing notably in size in the second five lines",{"_":54,"ana":55,"ref":56},{"lettering":157,"dimensions":158},"The letters are engraved in a fairly plain, square fashion, with simple serifs. Alpha is mostly with broken bar, sometimes with an extended upper serif, although there is a straight bar example in line 7 and in lines 8 and 10 straight bar descending to left foot; beta is closed, with larger lower eye, generally horizontal along the base; delta varies between regular triangle and oblique lower bar with extended serif above; epsilon has straight bars of equal length, except for instances in lines 9 and 10 when it is lunate; theta is ovoid with connecting straight bar; kappa has short tails; lambda sometimes has an extended upper serif; mu varies between a form with vertical first and last hastae and short middle strokes meeting above the line and cursive form comparable to a lower-case mu in line 9; omicron is full size in the first few lines, but increasingly is smaller and mid-line; sigma is consistently lunate, but more often formed of three straight strokes; less often a single curved stroke; omega is consistently lunate, and sometimes smaller and mid-line. The eta and nu are in ligature in lines 5, 6 and 7. In line 5 the omicron in the final word is inscribed above the other letters (due to omission?). The last two/three words of the last line are enclosed between a pair of christograms. Small hedera occur in lines 1, 3, 5, and 10.",[159,163,168,173,178,181,187,192,197,202,208,211,215,218,222,226,228,232,235],{"type":63,"l":64,"from":65,"to":65,"h":160,"unit":66,"atLeast":161,"atMost":162},"12-18","12","18",{"type":63,"l":164,"from":70,"to":70,"h":165,"unit":66,"atLeast":166,"atMost":167},"Line 2","14-19","14","19",{"type":63,"l":169,"from":170,"to":170,"h":171,"unit":66,"atLeast":161,"atMost":172},"Line 3","line3","12-22","22",{"type":63,"l":174,"from":175,"to":175,"h":176,"unit":66,"atLeast":177,"atMost":172},"Line 4","line4","8-22","8",{"type":63,"l":179,"from":180,"to":180,"h":160,"unit":66,"atLeast":161,"atMost":162},"Line 5","line5",{"type":63,"l":182,"from":183,"to":183,"h":184,"unit":66,"atLeast":185,"atMost":186},"Line 6","line6","9-16","9","16",{"type":63,"l":188,"from":189,"to":189,"h":190,"unit":66,"atLeast":191,"atMost":166},"Line 7","line7","7-14","7",{"type":63,"l":193,"from":194,"to":194,"h":195,"unit":66,"atLeast":196,"atMost":161},"Line 8","line8","6-12","6",{"type":63,"l":198,"from":199,"to":199,"h":200,"unit":66,"atLeast":196,"atMost":201},"Line 9","line9","6-10","10",{"type":63,"l":203,"from":204,"to":204,"h":205,"unit":66,"atLeast":206,"atMost":207},"Line 10","line10","5-13","5","13",{"type":68,"l":69,"from":65,"to":70,"h